@startuml
title GET /api/v1/pods/{pod_id}/stats/colors
hide footbox
actor Client
participant "FastAPI / Pydantic" as API
participant "SQLAlchemy session" as DB
database PostgreSQL as PG
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/pods/{pod_id}/stats/colors
API -> API: Validate positive pod_id
API -> DB: get_db(): request transaction
ref over API, DB: Clerk identity and route permissions (auth.puml)
DB -> PG: Find pod; missing -> 404
DB -> PG: Join players, games and results scoped to pod
DB -> PG: Normalize case/order/duplicates of WUBRG; explicit C = colorless
DB -> PG: Exclude null/blank/invalid identities
DB -> PG: Group canonical identities; count appearances, wins and draws
PG --> DB: At most 32 combination aggregates
DB --> API: Aggregate rows
API -> API: Sort combinations; roll up individual color counts
API -> API: win_rate = round(100 * wins / appearances, 2)
API -> API: Validate / serialize colors and combinations
API -> DB: Finish successful request
DB -> PG: COMMIT
API --> Client: 200 {colors, combinations}
note over API, PG
Only observed identities returned; unknown-only data gives empty lists.
Stored values and write contracts remain unchanged.
Draws count in the denominator. Shared errors: transaction.puml.
end note
@enduml
